From db539bce7aa294585540f0c46d017cd118164302 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:34:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sessions): a typed send takes over a chat another window
 holds only for a background turn [daveey]

An idle second Desktop (the always-on Mac mini) keeps chats loaded on its hub backend. After every
hub core update the MacBook backend restarts and drops its lease; the next Kanban notice, finished
background process or post-update continuation then runs in the mini backend, which takes the chat.
The user typing on the MacBook got "This chat is open somewhere else" several times a day.

prompt.submit now flags such a SESSION_NOT_OWNED refusal auto_take_over (with holder_turn_kind) when
the chat's newest live user row was started by Hermes: the turn-starting notice kinds
(agent.context_compressor_turns, minus the user's own loop_tick) plus auto_continue, including
untyped continuation notes recognised by their prefix as history does. The Desktop card then runs
its existing Take over here flow (session.take_over, transcript refresh, re-send) by itself, once
per fresh card: a card older than 30 s (a reopened chat) or a chat auto-taken in the last 2 min
waits for the click, so two windows cannot bounce a chat. A chat whose newest turn someone typed,
hidden/hosted sends and other refusals keep the card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
